---
import Adr from "../../components/Adr.astro";
import Layer from "../../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageLink from "../../components/PageLink.astro";
import Path from "../../components/Path.astro";
import Routes from "../../components/Routes.astro";
import Rule from "../../components/Rule.astro";

const M = "server/src/iki_server/runs/models.py";
const QU = "server/src/iki_server/runs/quotas.py";
const B = "server/src/iki_server/runs/budgets.py";
const C = "server/src/iki_server/runs/costs.py";

const H = {
  short: "What limits runs, and what they cost",
  how: "Where each limit applies",
  rules: "Quotas, budgets, costs and estimates",
  ref: "Routes, code and decisions",
};
const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: H.short },
  { id: "how", label: H.how },
  { id: "rules", label: H.rules },
  { id: "ref", label: H.ref },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title={H.short}>
    <p>
      Compute admins set quotas on how many runs may run and wait, per organization, team or
      project, on one tier or all. Machines Iki starts carry a price, so each container- and
      vm-tier run, and each call to a priced outside API, records what it cost and whose it was. A
      monthly budget warns as spending passes its thresholds, and an enforced one stops costly runs
      starting once it's spent (<Adr n={[45, 70, 71]} />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title={H.how}>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Limit</th><th>Checked</th><th>What happens past it</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>max_queued</code></td>
            <td>At launch, in its transaction, and again when a held run is approved</td>
            <td>The launch is refused, saying which scope is full (<Path p={QU} sym="def check_queued(" />).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>max_running</code></td>
            <td>At each lease, and when the provisioner counts what to start</td>
            <td>Jobs in that scope wait, even with a worker free; 0 pauses the scope (<Path p={QU} sym="def blocked(" />).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>An enforced budget</td>
            <td>At launch and approval; at each lease on a priced tier, or for runs calling priced APIs</td>
            <td>A spent budget refuses the launch, and stops its scope's queued costly runs starting (<Path p={B} sym="def check_launch(" />, <Path p={B} sym="def hold(" />).</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Every quota that covers a job applies, so a project's own limit and its team's both hold. The
      checks take an advisory lock while quotas exist for that tier, so two workers leasing at once
      can't both take the last slot. Leasing itself is on <PageLink to="The worker and its leases" />.
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={4} title={H.rules}>
    <div class="rules">
      <Rule title="Quotas" open>
        <p>
          A <code>RunQuota</code> has one scope (the organization, a team or a project), a tier or
          none for all tiers together, and either limit or both. <code>max_running</code> counts jobs
          workers hold; a packed job counts once, as it's one command on one worker (<Path
            p={M}
            sym="class RunQuota("
          />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="What a run costs">
        <p>
          Only the container and vm tiers have per-run costs; backend and self-hosted machines run
          anyway. An ephemeral machine's whole life, from being asked for to ending, is its run's. A
          persistent machine's time holding each attempt is that run's, and the rest is idle, the
          organization's. A packed job is split evenly between its runs. A Slurm job pays for what{" "}
          <code>sacct</code> says it used, at its template's rates, from when it started on its
          nodes. Each <code>CostRecord</code> keeps the price, project, team and action as they were,
          and is never changed (<Adr n="0070" />, <Path p={C} sym='PRICED_TIERS = ("container", "vm")' />,{" "}
          <Path p={M} sym="class CostRecord(" />).
        </p>
        <p>
          A call to an outside API costs the deployment's <code>ApiPrice</code> for it, on any tier
          (<Adr n="0130" />, <Path p={M} sym="class CostKind(" />). A run's page shows what it has
          cost so far, including machines still up (<Path p={C} sym="def of_run(" />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Budgets">
        <p>
          A <code>Budget</code> is a monthly amount for the organization, a team or a project, in
          calendar months in UTC. What's spent is what's recorded this month in its scope plus what
          machines still working for its runs have cost so far. As spending passes each of its{" "}
          <code>warn_at</code> percentages (50, 80 and 100 unless set), its Compute Admins, and a
          project's Admins for a project's budget, are told once a month each, and it's audited and
          sent to webhooks (<Adr n="0071" />, <Path p={B} sym="def send_alerts(" />).
        </p>
        <p>
          An enforced budget that's spent stops new container- and vm-tier runs, and runs calling
          priced outside APIs, in its scope until the month ends or it's raised. Runs already going
          finish. A launch whose runs' typical cost would take the budget past what's left is refused
          too.
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Estimates">
        <p>
          Before launching, an action on a priced tier shows the template it would run on, its price
          per hour, the median cost of its last 50 successful runs, and what a run would cost if it
          used its whole timeout (<Path p={C} sym="def estimate(" />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
    </div>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title={H.ref}>
    <h3>Routes</h3>
    <Routes paths={/^\/api\/v1\/compute\/(quotas|quota-scopes)/} />
    <Routes tags={["costs"]} />
    <div class="refs">
      <div>
        <h3>Where</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><Path p={QU} /></li>
          <li><Path p={B} /></li>
          <li><Path p={C} /></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Decisions</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><Adr n="0045" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0070" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0071" title /></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
